ilians ahead of winter. He also called the US president's waiver of new sanctions on Moscow a boost for Vladimir Putin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Police and protesters clash in nationwide protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7ccd2843afb5f720128fc3604596c61e7d0084ca6b011d6f91bbaf424056c6a</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:37:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-police-and-protesters-clash-in-nationwide-protests/a-79685584--b8149d16e8c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-police-and-protesters-clash-in-nationwide-protests/a-79685584?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Students, trade unionists and Yellow Vest activists are taking to French streets to protest high prices and inequality. Police and protesters have already clashed in Paris and Marseille.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Oregon school shooting: Police praise 'heroism' of those who intervened to stop more killing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ff010c85a51f70ffa5cbd355dd7f94d4c5884d95fde71860092f98aed1ab6ff</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T06:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-police-praise-heroism-of-those-who-intervened-to-stop-more-killing/a-79685302--68385910c32e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-police-praise-heroism-of-those-who-intervened-to-stop-more-killing/a-79685302?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US police have praised the actions of three people who cut short a deadly shooting at a school in the state of Oregon. Three children and a teacher were killed in the attack, carried out by a former pupil at the school.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian President Zelenskyy speaks at EU summit amid spat with Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f656e6e8bde153553b3ef29cfa22355dfa94556d4466448320c182f39629e04b</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340--6307cb90b3ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders reaffirmed support for Ukraine at the Brussels summit. But souring relations with the US over Russia and Starlink and a big hole in the budget will make for a difficult winter for Ukraine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hijab ban at schools in Azerbaijan: What's behind the rare wave of protests?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08ebefd989d279c7be8699b86c416fc4866a118bd15967d23e1ab967dd6a79f8</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T17:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716--35e52a17baf3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hijab-ban-at-schools-in-azerbaijan-what-s-behind-the-rare-wave-of-protests/a-79683716?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Girls wearing headscarves have been turned away from schools in Azerbaijan, triggering unusual protests involving children. The government rules do not mention hijabs. Why are schools enforcing unwritten rules?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Femicide in Iran: When 'honor' becomes a death sentence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e70ec12e69a3d634a90ae7d601733e95496e55ee70bcf865e50bbc3404284390</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/femicide-in-iran-when-honor-becomes-a-death-sentence/a-79681977--41194eafafb5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/femicide-in-iran-when-honor-becomes-a-death-sentence/a-79681977?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The murder of a young mother has once again sparked debate in Iran over so-called honor killings, the social acceptance of violence against women and the lack of protection for people vulnerable to gender-based violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: Students demand political change and resignation of Prime Minister Edi Rama</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e6b76fb4fa12c82c69b6c4b8e1290c306190a1068579f181eda4eae02854d93</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217--699ae649993b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-students-demand-political-change-and-resignation-of-prime-minister-edi-rama/a-79682217?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Empty lecture halls, burning buildings and demands for change: Albanian students are spearheading a protest movement that has become the biggest challenge to Prime Minister Edi Rama in years.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi attacks on strategic Saudi assets threaten Riyadh's regional leadership and economic ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01e1104c0b03745f3d8d2b1bd17453f9e2d31d3fd71502c88cd3421f8e368db3</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/houthi-attacks-on-strategic-saudi-assets-threaten-riyadh-s-regional-leadership-and-economic-ambition/a-79680200--af5776370a6d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/houthi-attacks-on-strategic-saudi-assets-threaten-riyadh-s-regional-leadership-and-economic-ambitions/a-79680200?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Yemen's Iran-backed Houthis continue to target Saudi Arabia, Riyadh's vulnerability threatens its claim on regional and religious leadership — as well as its standing as an economic powerhouse.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The EU wants an AI revolution. But on whose terms?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e799b1d2304f4fa4c2b48b3868c4eb173223aa6873797819cb940269137d24d</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456--ab198d15d72f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-eu-wants-an-ai-revolution-but-on-whose-terms/a-79673456?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the US and China race ahead, the European Union seeks to boost its economy with AI. Can it compete while protecting workers, safety and the climate?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India's young workers have a new colleague: AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2114fef6d81f43d5db8407f6c73d5c616c541f745a592410f7be15bd77ecd76</id><updated>2026-10-17T18:35:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T11:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-young-workers-have-a-new-colleague-ai/a-79678342--60612fda0623.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-young-workers-have-a-new-colleague-ai/a-79678342?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Artificial intelligence is changing the way Indian workplaces operate — raising questions about productivity, skills and entry-level jobs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
